{"id":"bs02","name":"Lifetime Listening Counts","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>A music app keeps lifetime listening counts. You have two tables.</p>\n<p><b>history</b> contains, for each user and song, the number of times the user has listened to the song so far (one row per pair):</p>\n<ul><li><code>user_id</code>, <code>song_id</code> - the pair;</li><li><code>tally</code> - the lifetime count (integer).</li></ul>\n<p><b>plays</b> is an event log with one row each time a user listens to a song:</p>\n<ul><li><code>user_id</code>, <code>song_id</code> - the pair;</li><li><code>played_at</code> - the timestamp of the play.</li></ul>\n<p><code>history</code> is up to date until the end of the day <b>before</b> the latest day of <code>plays</code>. Only the plays whose date is the latest date present in <code>plays</code> must be added; older plays are already counted.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return the updated lifetime counts with the columns <code>user_id</code>, <code>song_id</code> and <code>tally</code>, for every pair of <code>history</code> and every new pair of the latest day, sorted by <code>user_id</code>, then <code>song_id</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>Table <code>history</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>user_id</th><th>song_id</th><th>tally</th></tr><tr><td>shaw</td><td>rise</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>linda</td><td>lemon</td><td>4</td></tr></table></div><p>Table <code>plays</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>user_id</th><th>song_id</th><th>played_at</th></tr><tr><td>shaw</td><td>rise</td><td>2026-03-01 05:33:08</td></tr><tr><td>shaw</td><td>rise</td><td>2026-03-01 16:00:00</td></tr><tr><td>shaw</td><td>goodie</td><td>2026-03-01 10:15:00</td></tr><tr><td>linda</td><td>lemon</td><td>2026-02-28 00:00:00</td></tr><tr><td>mark</td><td>game</td><td>2026-03-01 04:00:00</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>user_id</th><th>song_id</th><th>tally</th></tr><tr><td>linda</td><td>lemon</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>mark</td><td>game</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>shaw</td><td>goodie</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>shaw</td><td>rise</td><td>4</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\nSELECT user_id, song_id, tally FROM history;\n","hints":["Agrège d'abord plays du dernier jour (GROUP BY user_id, song_id), PUIS joins à history : sinon tu multiplies les lignes.","FULL OUTER JOIN + COALESCE(h.tally, 0) + COALESCE(p.n, 0) pour garder les anciennes et les nouvelles paires."],"summary_fr":"Ajouter aux compteurs cumulés (history) les écoutes du dernier jour présent dans plays, y compris les nouvelles paires utilisateur-chanson.","tags":["agrégat puis jointure","FULL JOIN","COALESCE","filtre sur le dernier jour"],"minutes":15,"source":"shawlu95/Beyond-LeetCode-SQL (MIT) · Listening History","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"history":{"columns":[["user_id","VARCHAR(20)"],["song_id","VARCHAR(20)"],["tally","INT"]],"rows":[["shaw","rise",2],["linda","lemon",4]]},"plays":{"columns":[["user_id","VARCHAR(20)"],["song_id","VARCHAR(20)"],["played_at","TIMESTAMP"]],"rows":[["shaw","rise","2026-03-01 05:33:08"],["shaw","rise","2026-03-01 16:00:00"],["shaw","goodie","2026-03-01 10:15:00"],["linda","lemon","2026-02-28 00:00:00"],["mark","game","2026-03-01 04:00:00"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["user_id","song_id","tally"],"rows":[["linda","lemon",4],["mark","game",1],["shaw","goodie",1],["shaw","rise",4]]}},{"input":{"tables":{"history":{"columns":[["user_id","VARCHAR(20)"],["song_id","VARCHAR(20)"],["tally","INT"]],"rows":[["a","s1",10],["b","s2",1]]},"plays":{"columns":[["user_id","VARCHAR(20)"],["song_id","VARCHAR(20)"],["played_at","TIMESTAMP"]],"rows":[["a","s1","2026-03-04 23:59:59"],["a","s1","2026-03-05 00:00:00"],["b","s3","2026-03-05 08:00:00"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["user_id","song_id","tally"],"rows":[["a","s1",11],["b","s2",1],["b","s3",1]]}}],"hidden_n":6,"hidden":"","solution":""}